From 7aee160d2fc6f0ed4cfb8ac0bc79f07e3b309b12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 12:39:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] aggregation: a slot is given up to a holder the composition
 does not have yet

Slot selection took the strongest claim for each slot independently. When one
agent happened to be strongest in two slots, the composition rested on two
holders, and a rule asking for min_agents 3 / min_teams 2 refused it -- while
the same candidate set contained a selection with three agents in three teams.
The refused conclusion was supportable, so this was lost recall, not enforced
safety. It was found during the adversarial review of the 3-owner fixture and
recorded as "not fixed" in the research report.

After the strongest-per-slot pick, each slot whose holder also fills another
selected slot is now offered the best-ordered candidate whose holder is not
already in the selection. A swap is taken only when it raises the number of
distinct holders -- never to break a tie -- so a composition that is already
independent keeps exactly the claims it had, and the strongest claim still wins
every slot it does not double up on. Passes are bounded by the slot count and
the candidate order is total, so selection stays deterministic.

tests/independence_selection.rs, over the in-process transport with real SQLite
(no broker needed):
- the defect: log-1 strongest in two slots, sales-1 weaker in one of them.
  Before: 0 compositions. After: 1, support 3, teams 3, and the lineage carries
  sales-1's note, not log-1's second one.
- the control: when every slot already has its own holder, the strongest claim
  per slot is kept and a weaker note from the same agent is not taken. Passes
  before and after.

Based on a09283a. Prepared against a pinned commit because this session has
read-only access to this repository; the patch and these instructions are
committed to the continuation branch in anovruzov/NeuralGraph.

